    76	FIGURE 1: The Systematic Mapping Process
    77	The essential process steps of our systematic mapping study are deﬁnition of research questions,
    78	conducting the search for relevant papers, screening of papers, keywording of abstracts and data
    79	extraction and mapping (see Figure 1). Each process steps has an outcome, the ﬁnal outcome of
    80	the process being the systematic map.
    81	2.1. Deﬁnition of Research Questions (Research Scope)
    82	The main goal of a systematic mapping studies is to provide an overview of a research area,
    83	and identify the quantity and type of research and results available within it. Often one wants to
    84	map the frequencies of publication over time to see trends. A secondary goal can be to identify
    85	the forums in which research in the area has been published. These goals are reﬂected in both
